If a patient has an opioid-use then every clinician should advise an increased-hydration with the patient for a constipation-prevention.
If a patient has an opioid-use then every clinician should advise an increased-fiber-intake with the patient for a constipation-prevention.
If a patient has an opioid-use and a physical-activity-maintenance is possible for the patient then every clinician should advise a maintained-or-increased-physical-activity with the patient for a constipation-prevention.
